# Portfolio AWS - Deployment Guide

## Prerequisites

- AWS Account com Free Tier ativo
- AWS CLI v2 configurado
- Python 3.8+
- Git
- Bash shell

## Step 1: Clone/Download do Repositório

```bash
# Se for via GitHub
git clone <seu-repo>
cd portfolio

# Ou extrair o arquivo ZIP
unzip portfolio.zip
cd portfolio
```

## Step 2: Configurar AWS CLI

```bash
# Configurar credenciais
aws configure

# Confirmar
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

## Step 3: Deploy Infrastructure

### 3.1 Criar S3 Buckets

```bash
cd infrastructure
chmod +x *.sh

./create-buckets.sh

# Salvar a saída (bucket names)
# Exemplo de output esperado:
# Website Bucket: portfolio-website-1234567890
# Assets Bucket: portfolio-assets-1234567890
```

### 3.2 Upload dos Arquivos Website

```bash
# Atualizar as variáveis com os buckets criados
export WEBSITE_BUCKET="portfolio-website-XXXXXXXXX"
export ASSETS_BUCKET="portfolio-assets-XXXXXXXXX"

# Upload website files
aws s3 sync ../website/ s3://$WEBSITE_BUCKET/ \
  --delete \
  --exclude "images/*" \
  --exclude "docs/*" \
  --cache-control "max-age=86400"

# Upload images
aws s3 sync ../website/images/ s3://$WEBSITE_BUCKET/images/ \
  --cache-control "max-age=31536000"
```

### 3.3 Configurar CloudFront

```bash
# Criar distribuição CloudFront
./setup-cloudfront.sh

# Salvar o DISTRIBUTION_ID da saída
# Esperado: Distribution ID: E1234567890ABC
```

### 3.4 Configurar Políticas de Segurança

```bash
# Configurar bucket policies
./configure-policies.sh
```

## Step 4: Deploy Lambda Functions

### 4.1 Contact Form Lambda

```bash
cd ../lambda/contact-form

# Criar arquivo ZIP
pip install -r requirements.txt -t .
zip -r function.zip . -x "*.pyc"

# Deploy
aws lambda create-function \
  --function-name portfolio-contact-form \
  --runtime python3.11 \
  --role arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:role/service-role/lambda-role \
  --handler index.lambda_handler \
  --zip-file fileb://function.zip \
  --timeout 30 \
  --memory-size 256 \
  --environment Variables="{DYNAMODB_TABLE=portfolio-contacts,SENDER_EMAIL=seu@email.com}"

# Salvar FUNCTION_ARN
```

### 4.2 Image Processor Lambda

```bash
cd ../image-processor

# Setup
pip install -r requirements.txt -t .
zip -r function.zip . -x "*.pyc"

# Deploy
aws lambda create-function \
  --function-name portfolio-image-processor \
  --runtime python3.11 \
  --role arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:role/service-role/lambda-role \
  --handler index.lambda_handler \
  --zip-file fileb://function.zip \
  --timeout 60 \
  --memory-size 512 \
  --environment Variables="{ASSETS_BUCKET=$ASSETS_BUCKET}"
```

## Step 5: Setup DynamoDB

```bash
# Criar tabela de contatos
aws dynamodb create-table \
  --table-name portfolio-contacts \
  --attribute-definitions \
    AttributeName=contact_id,AttributeType=S \
  --key-schema \
    AttributeName=contact_id,KeyType=HASH \
  --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST
```

## Step 6: Setup API Gateway

```bash
# Criar API REST
aws apigateway create-rest-api \
  --name portfolio-api \
  --description "Portfolio Contact API"

# Nota: Configuração completa requer múltiplos passos
# Recomenda-se usar AWS Console ou CloudFormation
```

## Step 7: Configure SES (Optional)

```bash
# Verificar email (produção)
aws ses verify-email-identity --email-address seu@email.com

# Verificar domínio (produção)
aws ses verify-domain-identity --domain seu-domain.com
```

## Step 8: Verificar Deployment

```bash
# Testar CloudFront
curl -I https://your-cloudfront-domain.cloudfront.net

# Testar S3
aws s3 ls s3://$WEBSITE_BUCKET/

# Testar Lambda
aws lambda invoke \
  --function-name portfolio-contact-form \
  --payload file://test-payload.json \
  response.json
```

